// (),int) to discourage early EOS while the expression is short. We also
// limit the unconstrained preamble to `prefixBudget` steps and force-open one
// constrained span if the model never emits `<<` naturally (20/49 no-span
// failures). After EOS we close with `CloseConstrainedSpan` (if complete) or
// `CloseSpanWithinBudget` (if incomplete), guaranteeing `>>` is emitted before
// budget exhaustion. Multiple `<<…>>` spans are handled by continuing the outer
// loop after each close, but force-open fires at most once (`everInsideSpan`
// guard). Guidance is sharpened to require the exact final-answer line.
