//     both set currentConstrainedOut := [] which satisfies IsValidPrefix([]) by
//     precondition parser.IsValidPrefix([]). The implication is vacuous while
//     outside the span.
//   Inside branch (non-EOS): `SafeBoostedConstrainedStep` returns only parser-
//     valid tokens or EOS (hard-mask postcondition). `AppendConstrainedToken`
//     extends currentConstrainedOut by that valid token and its postcondition
//     preserves IsValidPrefix. Invariant maintained.
//   Inside branch (EOS, complete close): `CloseConstrainedSpan` sets
//     insideConstrainedOut := false, making the implication vacuously true.
//   Inside branch (EOS, incomplete close): `CloseSpanWithinBudget` postcondition
//     guarantees insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut), so the
//     invariant is preserved regardless of whether the span was closed.
//
// progress (|generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps):
//   Outside step: appends at most 1 token (EOS is not appended) and steps += 1.
//   Force-open: `OpenConstrainedSpan` appends "<<" (1 token) and steps += 1.
//   Inside (non-EOS): `SafeBoostedConstrainedStep` costs 1 step (steps += 1),
//     `AppendConstrainedToken` appends 1 token. Net: +1 step, +1 visible token.
//   Inside (EOS then close): the EOS step costs 1 (steps += 1); `CloseConstrainedSpan`
//     appends ">>" (1 token) and costs 1 (steps += 1). Two steps, two tokens max.
//     Since close is guarded by steps < maxSteps, total steps <= maxSteps.
//   Inside (EOS then CloseSpanWithinBudget): budget cb = maxSteps - steps;
